#: ../../library/collections.rst:1046
msgid ""
"Since a named tuple is a regular Python class, it is easy to add or change "
"functionality with a subclass.  Here is how to add a calculated field and a "
"fixed-width print format:"
msgstr ""
"Da ein benanntes Tupel eine normale Python-Klasse ist, lässt sich "
"Funktionalität mit einer Unterklasse leicht hinzufügen oder ändern. So fügst "
"du ein berechnetes Feld und ein Druckformat mit fester Breite hinzu:"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1050
msgid ""
">>> class Point(namedtuple('Point', ['x', 'y'])):\n"
"...     __slots__ = ()\n"
"...     @property\n"
"...     def hypot(self):\n"
"...         return (self.x ** 2 + self.y ** 2) ** 0.5\n"
"...     def __str__(self):\n"
"...         return 'Point: x=%6.3f  y=%6.3f  hypot=%6.3f' % (self.x, self.y, "
"self.hypot)\n"
"\n"
">>> for p in Point(3, 4), Point(14, 5/7):\n"
"...     print(p)\n"
"Point: x= 3.000  y= 4.000  hypot= 5.000\n"
"Point: x=14.000  y= 0.714  hypot=14.018"
msgstr ""
">>> class Point(namedtuple('Point', ['x', 'y'])):\n"
"...     __slots__ = ()\n"
"...     @property\n"
"...     def hypot(self):\n"
"...         return (self.x ** 2 + self.y ** 2) ** 0.5\n"
"...     def __str__(self):\n"
"...         return 'Point: x=%6.3f  y=%6.3f  hypot=%6.3f' % (self.x, self.y, "
"self.hypot)\n"
"\n"
">>> for p in Point(3, 4), Point(14, 5/7):\n"
"...     print(p)\n"
"Point: x= 3.000  y= 4.000  hypot= 5.000\n"
"Point: x=14.000  y= 0.714  hypot=14.018"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1065
msgid ""
"The subclass shown above sets ``__slots__`` to an empty tuple.  This helps "
"keep memory requirements low by preventing the creation of instance "
"dictionaries."
msgstr ""
"Die oben gezeigte Unterklasse setzt ``__slots__`` auf ein leeres Tupel. Das "
"hilft, den Speicherbedarf gering zu halten, indem die Erzeugung von "
"Instanz-Dictionaries verhindert wird."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1068
msgid ""
"Subclassing is not useful for adding new, stored fields.  Instead, simply "
