msgstr ":class:`OrderedDict`-Beispiele und -Rezepte"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1218
msgid ""
"It is straightforward to create an ordered dictionary variant that remembers "
"the order the keys were *last* inserted. If a new entry overwrites an "
"existing entry, the original insertion position is changed and moved to the "
"end::"
msgstr ""
"Es ist einfach, eine Variante eines geordneten Dictionaries zu erstellen, "
"die sich die Reihenfolge merkt, in der die Schlüssel *zuletzt* eingefügt "
"wurden. Überschreibt ein neuer Eintrag einen vorhandenen, wird die "
"ursprüngliche Einfügeposition geändert und ans Ende verschoben::"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1223
msgid ""
"class LastUpdatedOrderedDict(OrderedDict):\n"
"    'Store items in the order that the keys were last updated.'\n"
"\n"
"    def __setitem__(self, key, value):\n"
"        super().__setitem__(key, value)\n"
"        self.move_to_end(key)"
msgstr ""
"class LastUpdatedOrderedDict(OrderedDict):\n"
"    'Store items in the order that the keys were last updated.'\n"
"\n"
"    def __setitem__(self, key, value):\n"
"        super().__setitem__(key, value)\n"
"        self.move_to_end(key)"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1230
msgid ""
"An :class:`OrderedDict` would also be useful for implementing variants "
"of :deco:`functools.lru_cache`:"
msgstr ""
"Ein :class:`OrderedDict` wäre auch nützlich, um Varianten von "
":deco:`functools.lru_cache` zu implementieren:"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1233
msgid ""
"from collections import OrderedDict\n"
"from time import monotonic\n"
"\n"
"class TimeBoundedLRU:\n"
"    \"LRU Cache that invalidates and refreshes old entries.\"\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self, func, maxsize=128, maxage=30):\n"
"        self.cache = OrderedDict()      # { args : (timestamp, result)}\n"
"        self.func = func\n"
"        self.maxsize = maxsize\n"
"        self.maxage = maxage\n"
"\n"
"    def __call__(self, *args):\n"
"        if args in self.cache:\n"
"            self.cache.move_to_end(args)\n"
"            timestamp, result = self.cache[args]\n"
"            if monotonic() - timestamp <= self.maxage:\n"
"                return result\n"
"        result = self.func(*args)\n"
"        self.cache[args] = monotonic(), result\n"
"        if len(self.cache) > self.maxsize:\n"
"            self.cache.popitem(last=False)\n"
"        return result"
msgstr ""
"from collections import OrderedDict\n"
"from time import monotonic\n"
"\n"
"class TimeBoundedLRU:\n"
"    \"LRU Cache that invalidates and refreshes old entries.\"\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self, func, maxsize=128, maxage=30):\n"
"        self.cache = OrderedDict()      # { args : (timestamp, result)}\n"
"        self.func = func\n"
"        self.maxsize = maxsize\n"
"        self.maxage = maxage\n"
"\n"
"    def __call__(self, *args):\n"
"        if args in self.cache:\n"
"            self.cache.move_to_end(args)\n"
"            timestamp, result = self.cache[args]\n"
"            if monotonic() - timestamp <= self.maxage:\n"
"                return result\n"
"        result = self.func(*args)\n"
"        self.cache[args] = monotonic(), result\n"
"        if len(self.cache) > self.maxsize:\n"
"            self.cache.popitem(last=False)\n"
"        return result"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1260
msgid ""
"class MultiHitLRUCache:\n"
"    \"\"\" LRU cache that defers caching a result until\n"
"        it has been requested multiple times.\n"
"\n"
"        To avoid flushing the LRU cache with one-time requests,\n"
"        we don't cache until a request has been made more than once.\n"
"\n"
"    \"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self, func, maxsize=128, maxrequests=4096, cache_after=1):\n"
"        self.requests = OrderedDict()   # { uncached_key : request_count }\n"
"        self.cache = OrderedDict()      # { cached_key : function_result }\n"
"        self.func = func\n"
"        self.maxrequests = maxrequests  # max number of uncached requests\n"
"        self.maxsize = maxsize          # max number of stored return "
"values\n"
"        self.cache_after = cache_after\n"
"\n"
"    def __call__(self, *args):\n"
"        if args in self.cache:\n"
"            self.cache.move_to_end(args)\n"
"            return self.cache[args]\n"
"        result = self.func(*args)\n"
"        self.requests[args] = self.requests.get(args, 0) + 1\n"
"        if self.requests[args] <= self.cache_after:\n"
"            self.requests.move_to_end(args)\n"
"            if len(self.requests) > self.maxrequests:\n"
"                self.requests.popitem(last=False)\n"
"        else:\n"
"            self.requests.pop(args, None)\n"
"            self.cache[args] = result\n"
"            if len(self.cache) > self.maxsize:\n"
"                self.cache.popitem(last=False)\n"
"        return result"
msgstr ""
"class MultiHitLRUCache:\n"
"    \"\"\" LRU cache that defers caching a result until\n"
"        it has been requested multiple times.\n"
"\n"
"        To avoid flushing the LRU cache with one-time requests,\n"
"        we don't cache until a request has been made more than once.\n"
"\n"
"    \"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self, func, maxsize=128, maxrequests=4096, cache_after=1):\n"
"        self.requests = OrderedDict()   # { uncached_key : request_count }\n"
"        self.cache = OrderedDict()      # { cached_key : function_result }\n"
"        self.func = func\n"
"        self.maxrequests = maxrequests  # max number of uncached requests\n"
"        self.maxsize = maxsize          # max number of stored return "
"values\n"
"        self.cache_after = cache_after\n"
"\n"
"    def __call__(self, *args):\n"
"        if args in self.cache:\n"
"            self.cache.move_to_end(args)\n"
"            return self.cache[args]\n"
"        result = self.func(*args)\n"
"        self.requests[args] = self.requests.get(args, 0) + 1\n"
"        if self.requests[args] <= self.cache_after:\n"
"            self.requests.move_to_end(args)\n"
"            if len(self.requests) > self.maxrequests:\n"
"                self.requests.popitem(last=False)\n"
"        else:\n"
"            self.requests.pop(args, None)\n"
"            self.cache[args] = result\n"
"            if len(self.cache) > self.maxsize:\n"
"                self.cache.popitem(last=False)\n"
"        return result"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1329
msgid ":class:`UserDict` objects"
msgstr ":class:`UserDict`-Objekte"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1331
msgid ""
"The class, :class:`UserDict` acts as a wrapper around dictionary objects. "
"The need for this class has been partially supplanted by the ability to "
"subclass directly from :class:`dict`; however, this class can be easier to "
"work with because the underlying dictionary is accessible as an attribute."
msgstr ""
"Die Klasse :class:`UserDict` fungiert als Wrapper um Dictionary-Objekte. Der "
"Bedarf an dieser Klasse wurde teilweise dadurch ersetzt, dass man direkt von "
":class:`dict` ableiten kann. Diese Klasse kann jedoch einfacher zu handhaben "
"sein, weil das zugrunde liegende Dictionary als Attribut zugänglich ist."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1341
msgid ""
"Class that simulates a dictionary.  The instance's contents are kept in a "
"regular dictionary, which is accessible via the :attr:`data` attribute "
"of :class:`!UserDict` instances.  If arguments are provided, they are used "
"to initialize :attr:`data`, like a regular dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Klasse, die ein Dictionary simuliert. Der Inhalt der Instanz wird in einem "
"normalen Dictionary gehalten, das über das Attribut :attr:`data` von "
":class:`!UserDict`-Instanzen zugänglich ist. Werden Argumente angegeben, "
"dienen sie wie bei einem normalen Dictionary zur Initialisierung von "
":attr:`data`."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1346
msgid ""
"In addition to supporting the methods and operations of mappings, :class:`!"
"UserDict` instances provide the following attribute:"
msgstr ""
"Zusätzlich zur Unterstützung der Methoden und Operationen von Mappings "
"bieten :class:`!UserDict`-Instanzen das folgende Attribut:"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1351
msgid ""
"A real dictionary used to store the contents of the :class:`UserDict` class."
msgstr ""
"Ein echtes Dictionary, in dem der Inhalt der Klasse :class:`UserDict` "
"gespeichert wird."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1354
msgid ":class:`!UserDict` instances also override the following method:"
msgstr ""
":class:`!UserDict`-Instanzen überschreiben außerdem die folgende Methode:"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1358
msgid ""
"Remove and return a ``(key, value)`` pair from the wrapped dictionary. Pairs "
"are returned in the same order as ``data.popitem()``. (For the "
"default :meth:`dict.popitem`, this order is :abbr:`LIFO (last-in, first-"
"out)`.) If the dictionary is empty, raises a :exc:`KeyError`."
msgstr ""
"Entfernt ein ``(key, value)``-Paar aus dem umhüllten Dictionary und gibt es "
"zurück. Die Paare werden in derselben Reihenfolge wie bei ``data.popitem()`` "
"zurückgegeben. (Beim Standard :meth:`dict.popitem` ist diese Reihenfolge "
":abbr:`LIFO (last-in, first-out)`.) Ist das Dictionary leer, wird ein "
":exc:`KeyError` ausgelöst."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1364
msgid ":class:`UserList` objects"
msgstr ":class:`UserList`-Objekte"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1366
msgid ""
"This class acts as a wrapper around list objects.  It is a useful base class "
"for your own list-like classes which can inherit from them and override "
"existing methods or add new ones.  In this way, one can add new behaviors to "
"lists."
msgstr ""
"Diese Klasse fungiert als Wrapper um Listenobjekte. Sie ist eine nützliche "
"Basisklasse für eigene listenähnliche Klassen, die von ihr erben und "
"bestehende Methoden überschreiben oder neue hinzufügen können. Auf diese "
"Weise lassen sich Listen neue Verhaltensweisen hinzufügen."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1371
msgid ""
"The need for this class has been partially supplanted by the ability to "
"subclass directly from :class:`list`; however, this class can be easier to "
"work with because the underlying list is accessible as an attribute."
msgstr ""
"Der Bedarf an dieser Klasse wurde teilweise dadurch ersetzt, dass man direkt "
"von :class:`list` ableiten kann. Diese Klasse kann jedoch einfacher zu "
"handhaben sein, weil die zugrunde liegende Liste als Attribut zugänglich ist."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1377
msgid ""
"Class that simulates a list.  The instance's contents are kept in a regular "
"list, which is accessible via the :attr:`data` attribute "
"of :class:`UserList` instances.  The instance's contents are initially set "
"to a copy of *list*, defaulting to the empty list ``[]``.  *list* can be any "
"iterable, for example a real Python list or a :class:`UserList` object."
msgstr ""
"Klasse, die eine Liste simuliert. Der Inhalt der Instanz wird in einer "
"normalen Liste gehalten, die über das Attribut :attr:`data` von "
":class:`UserList`-Instanzen zugänglich ist. Der Inhalt der Instanz wird "
"anfangs auf eine Kopie von *list* gesetzt, standardmäßig die leere Liste "
"``[]``. *list* kann jedes iterierbare Objekt sein, zum Beispiel eine echte "
"Python-Liste oder ein :class:`UserList`-Objekt."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1383
msgid ""
"In addition to supporting the methods and operations of mutable "
"sequences, :class:`UserList` instances provide the following attribute:"
msgstr ""
"Zusätzlich zur Unterstützung der Methoden und Operationen veränderlicher "
"Sequenzen bieten :class:`UserList`-Instanzen das folgende Attribut:"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1388
msgid ""
"A real :class:`list` object used to store the contents of "
"the :class:`UserList` class."
msgstr ""
"Ein echtes :class:`list`-Objekt, in dem der Inhalt der Klasse "
":class:`UserList` gespeichert wird."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1391
msgid ""
"**Subclassing requirements:** Subclasses of :class:`UserList` are expected "
"to offer a constructor which can be called with either no arguments or one "
"argument.  List operations which return a new sequence attempt to create an "
"instance of the actual implementation class.  To do so, it assumes that the "
"constructor can be called with a single parameter, which is a sequence "
"object used as a data source."
msgstr ""
"**Anforderungen an Unterklassen:** Von Unterklassen von :class:`UserList` "
"wird erwartet, dass sie einen Konstruktor anbieten, der entweder ohne "
"Argumente oder mit einem Argument aufgerufen werden kann. Listenoperationen, "
"die eine neue Sequenz zurückgeben, versuchen, eine Instanz der tatsächlichen "
"Implementierungsklasse zu erzeugen. Dazu wird angenommen, dass der "
"Konstruktor mit einem einzigen Parameter aufgerufen werden kann, der ein als "
"Datenquelle dienendes Sequenzobjekt ist."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1398
msgid ""
"If a derived class does not wish to comply with this requirement, all of the "
"special methods supported by this class will need to be overridden; please "
"consult the sources for information about the methods which need to be "
"provided in that case."
msgstr ""
"Möchte eine abgeleitete Klasse diese Anforderung nicht erfüllen, müssen alle "
"von dieser Klasse unterstützten speziellen Methoden überschrieben werden. "
"Informationen darüber, welche Methoden in diesem Fall bereitgestellt werden "
"müssen, findest du im Quellcode."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1404
msgid ":class:`UserString` objects"
msgstr ":class:`UserString`-Objekte"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1406
msgid ""
"The class, :class:`UserString` acts as a wrapper around string objects. The "
"need for this class has been partially supplanted by the ability to subclass "
"directly from :class:`str`; however, this class can be easier to work with "
"because the underlying string is accessible as an attribute."
msgstr ""
"Die Klasse :class:`UserString` fungiert als Wrapper um String-Objekte. Der "
"Bedarf an dieser Klasse wurde teilweise dadurch ersetzt, dass man direkt von "
":class:`str` ableiten kann. Diese Klasse kann jedoch einfacher zu handhaben "
"sein, weil der zugrunde liegende String als Attribut zugänglich ist."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1414
msgid ""
"Class that simulates a string object.  The instance's content is kept in a "
"regular string object, which is accessible via the :attr:`data` attribute "
"of :class:`UserString` instances.  The instance's contents are initially set "
"to a copy of *seq*.  The *seq* argument can be any object which can be "
"converted into a string using the built-in :func:`str` function."
msgstr ""
"Klasse, die ein String-Objekt simuliert. Der Inhalt der Instanz wird in "
"einem normalen String-Objekt gehalten, das über das Attribut :attr:`data` "
"von :class:`UserString`-Instanzen zugänglich ist. Der Inhalt der Instanz "
"wird anfangs auf eine Kopie von *seq* gesetzt. Das Argument *seq* kann jedes "
"Objekt sein, das sich mit der eingebauten Funktion :func:`str` in einen "
"String umwandeln lässt."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1421
msgid ""
"In addition to supporting the methods and operations of "
"strings, :class:`UserString` instances provide the following attribute:"
msgstr ""
"Zusätzlich zur Unterstützung der Methoden und Operationen von Strings bieten "
":class:`UserString`-Instanzen das folgende Attribut:"

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1426
msgid ""
"A real :class:`str` object used to store the contents of "
"the :class:`UserString` class."
msgstr ""
"Ein echtes :class:`str`-Objekt, in dem der Inhalt der Klasse "
":class:`UserString` gespeichert wird."

#: ../../library/collections.rst:1429
msgid ""
"New methods ``__getnewargs__``, ``__rmod__``, ``casefold``, ``format_map``, "
"``isprintable``, and ``maketrans``."
msgstr ""
"Neue Methoden ``__getnewargs__``, ``__rmod__``, ``casefold``, "
"``format_map``, ``isprintable`` und ``maketrans``."
